            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0241" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23661: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dyer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-20T09:00:00-07:23"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                                1920—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:48 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Governor wired me last night that he has ordered 50 soldiers to Cananea. General
                    Serrano here yesterday said States of Michoacán, <pb facs="0242" n="142"
                        xml:id="pg142"/> Hidalgo, Guerrero, Colima, Jalisco, Zacatecas and Tabasco
                    are openly favoring Sonora attitude.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dyer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
